WEBVTT

1
00:00:04.400 --> 00:00:08.765
Press a switch, and the lamp lights
up. Electricity makes it work.

2
00:00:08.985 --> 00:00:12.933
A magnet pulls a paperclip. It
does not even have to touch it.

3
00:00:13.433 --> 00:00:17.055
Some things need electricity
to work. Some do not.

4
00:00:17.275 --> 00:00:21.594
A lamp, a television, a fridge
and a phone all need electricity.

5
00:00:21.814 --> 00:00:24.415
A book, a chair and a bicycle do not.

6
00:00:24.635 --> 00:00:27.282
Here is the test. What
if the power went off?

7
00:00:27.502 --> 00:00:30.985
The lamp goes out. But you
can still read the book.

8
00:00:31.205 --> 00:00:35.338
If it stops when the power
goes off, it needs electricity.

9
00:00:35.838 --> 00:00:38.996
Electricity comes into
your house through wires.

10
00:00:39.216 --> 00:00:41.584
The wires go to the sockets in the wall.

11
00:00:41.804 --> 00:00:44.962
A plug takes it to the
lamp. The lamp lights up.

12
00:00:45.182 --> 00:00:48.758
A battery gives electricity
to torches and toys.

13
00:00:48.978 --> 00:00:52.461
So look for a plug on a
lead, or a battery inside.

14
00:00:52.961 --> 00:00:56.630
Electricity is very useful.
But it can hurt you.

15
00:00:56.850 --> 00:01:02.190
Rule one. Only plugs go into
sockets. Never fingers or toys.

16
00:01:02.410 --> 00:01:09.144
Rule two. Keep electric things away from
water. Wet hands and electricity do not mix.

17
00:01:09.364 --> 00:01:15.401
Rule three. If a wire is broken,
do not touch it. Tell a grown-up.

18
00:01:15.901 --> 00:01:19.942
A magnet attracts some things.
Attract means pull towards.

19
00:01:20.162 --> 00:01:23.645
Bring a magnet near a paperclip.
The clip jumps across!

20
00:01:23.865 --> 00:01:26.697
It jumps before the
magnet even touches it.

21
00:01:26.917 --> 00:01:29.704
Bring the magnet near
paper. Nothing happens.

22
00:01:29.924 --> 00:01:33.593
People often say a magnet
sticks. But glue sticks.

23
00:01:33.813 --> 00:01:39.803
Pull the clip off, and it comes away easily.
A magnet attracts, and lets go again.

24
00:01:40.303 --> 00:01:43.693
Test each thing, and write
the results in a table.

25
00:01:43.913 --> 00:01:48.047
The steel paperclip is attracted.
So is the steel tin lid.

26
00:01:48.267 --> 00:01:52.028
The wooden block is not
attracted. The plastic cup is not.

27
00:01:52.248 --> 00:01:56.381
Kitchen foil is metal. Predict:
will the magnet attract it?

28
00:01:56.601 --> 00:02:00.549
Test it. Nothing happens.
Not every metal is magnetic.

29
00:02:00.769 --> 00:02:04.530
Look at the table. A magnet
attracts iron and steel.

30
00:02:05.030 --> 00:02:09.489
Some things need electricity. It
comes from sockets and batteries.

31
00:02:09.709 --> 00:02:13.470
Only plugs in sockets. Away
from water. Tell a grown-up.

32
00:02:13.690 --> 00:02:18.056
A magnet attracts iron and steel.
Not every metal is magnetic.

33
00:02:18.276 --> 00:02:21.341
Now predict, then test, and
see the pattern for yourself.
